--
--   Description
--
-- Normal Gigabit Operation:
-- 1. Initialise the GEM by enabling receive, enabling gigabit mode, 
--      enabling the GMII interface, enabling the interrupts, 
--      writing to specific address register one with an address, and 
--      writing to the receive buffer queue pointer register with the 
--      initial location of the receive buffer pointer.
-- 2. Drive a good frame with minimum length plus extension into the 
--      GMII receive interface. Check the receive data and status as it 
--      is written to the AHB interface.
-- 3. Check the status registers, and statistic registers once the frame is 
--      completely received.  Ensure the frame was received properly with 
--      only the relevant status and statistic registers set.
--
-- Burst Gigabit Operation:
-- 4. In burst mode, drive a good frame with minimum length plus extension 
--      into the GMII receive interface. Next, drive two good minimum 
--      length frames. Finally, provide the receive buffer pointer to the 
--      AHB interface.
-- 5. Provide the receive buffer pointers to the AHB interface.
-- 6. Check the status registers, and statistic registers once the frame is 
--      completely received. Ensure the frame was received properly with only 
--      the relevant status and statistic registers set.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wait_states 0
pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 speed 0 --  check reset state

--******************************************************************************
-- Normal Gigabit Operation:

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbrd      30 00000000  -- check that all interrupts are now enabled
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      04 00080401  -- indicate 1G operation
apbrd      04 00080401  -- verify write to speed register..

-- check the external pins
pinsc(apb) loopback 0 half_duplex 1 speed 1  -- check speed pin

